content.text:
The telemetry points to one root cause: product-catalog. Its pod restarted and its spans and logs went silent, and the failures spread through checkout and recommendation to frontend and frontend-proxy. The postgresql and flagd memory shifts are small and don't line up with any error, so I'm not treating them as separate faults.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "product-catalog",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, count(*) AS n, min(time) AS t0, max(time) AS t1, avg(value) AS avgv, max(value) AS maxv FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'product-catalog%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "product-catalog pod restart counter rose to 1 in the abnormal window; it was 0 in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, date_trunc('minute', time) AS m, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'product-catalog' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 2", "claim": "product-catalog emits only 2 spans in the abnormal window, versus about 600 in normal, and none after 05:21."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, max(time) AS last_log, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name = 'product-catalog' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "product-catalog logs stop at about 05:21:59, just before its restart and the frontend error onset."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "product-catalog", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name LIKE '%ProductCatalogService/GetProduct' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "frontend's gRPC GetProduct calls to product-catalog almost all error (136 of 137) in the abnormal window."}]},
    {"from": "product-catalog", "to": "recommendation", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'recommendation' AND span_name LIKE '%ProductCatalogService/ListProducts' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "recommendation's ListProducts calls to product-catalog all fail (29 of 29) in the abnormal window."}]},
    {"from": "product-catalog", "to": "checkout", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind AS kind, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'checkout' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "checkout's GetProduct client calls to product-catalog fail (19 of 19), and PlaceOrder fails with them."}]},
    {"from": "checkout", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name LIKE '%CheckoutService/PlaceOrder' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "frontend's PlaceOrder calls to checkout fail on every request (19 of 19) in the abnormal window."}]},
    {"from": "recommendation", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name LIKE '%api/recommendations%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "frontend /api/recommendations returns HTTP 500 on all 29 requests in the abnormal window."}]},
    {"from": "frontend", "to": "frontend-proxy", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend-proxy' AND span_name = 'ingress' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "frontend-proxy ingress returns 500 on 208 requests in the abnormal window, versus 20 in normal."}]}
  ]
}
